description: "The right-to-left override (U+202E) character lets an attacker craft a filename that displays as a harmless text document while the real executable extension sits at the end. A file named invoice‮txt.sh is shown by file managers as invoice‮sh.txt, hiding the shell-script nature from users. This demo ships a real shell script with the RLO-spoofed filename and a clean counterpart. FileType Engine verifies the true magic bytes behind the displayed name, so the masquerade is exposed regardless of what the file manager renders.",
