    title: "Archive locale metadata contradicting embedded document language",
    titleZh: "封存檔地區設定與內嵌文件語言相互矛盾",
    description: "Masquerading can happen at the container level as well as in the payload. An archive's locale and language metadata — the region, codepage, or comment language — can be deliberately set to mislead, while the documents it contains tell a different story. A file that claims a benign origin but embeds content in an unexpected language or encoding is a red flag worth scrutiny, since attackers often forge metadata to evade geo-based triage and appear trustworthy. In this demo a benign RAR/ZIP sample presents conflicting locale and content-language signals. The Country of Origin module compares container metadata against the language and structure of the embedded documents, exposing the discrepancy. The mismatch is surfaced clearly so analysts can decide whether the file is legitimate or deliberately disguised.",
    descriptionZh: "偽裝不僅發生在承載層次，也可能出現在容器層次。封存檔的地區設定與語言中繼資料——例如地區、字碼頁或註解語言——可能被刻意設定以誤導他人，而其中所含的文件卻呈現不同訊息。一個自稱來自無害來源、卻嵌入意料之外語言或編碼內容的檔案，是值得警惕的紅旗；攻擊者常竄改這類中繼資料，以繞過以地理區域為依據的分流，並使自己看似可信。本示範以良性 RAR/ZIP 樣本呈現相互矛盾的地區設定與內容語言訊號。Country of Origin 模組會比對容器中繼資料與所嵌入文件的語言與結構，揭露其中的落差。這項不一致會清楚浮現，讓分析人員判斷檔案究竟是合法的，還是刻意偽裝。",
